node_modules/
dist/
.codex-tmp/
.env
.env.*
*.env

# ── Datos de cliente: NUNCA salen del disco local ────────────────────────────
# Regla negativa por defecto. Los LCM, exports y snapshots son sistemas
# financieros de clientes reales: no van a ningún remoto, ni siquiera privado.
clients/**
!clients/.gitkeep

# The rule above contains a slash, so git anchors it to the repo root and a nested
# clients/ directory walks straight past it. packages/engagement/clients/convex held a
# real engagement report - hours per renewal, invoice INV20958 and its amounts - and was
# one `git add -A` away from a company-wide org. Rule 1 says client data never leaves
# clients/; this is what actually enforces it at any depth.
**/clients/**
